  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts based on docs recipe 3 (skinned character with crossfade). It passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser here, so none of the runtime behavior below has been seen working.\n\n- **Scene:** `/assets/soldier.glb` loads through `defineModelAssets` at 1.8 m height on a 12×12 ground plane. A perspective camera frames it, and one shadow-casting directional light plus a hemisphere fill light it.\n- **Animation:** it starts on `Idle`. `R` crossfades to `Run` and `I` crossfades back to `Idle`, each over 0.4 s.\n- **`window.__EVAL__`:** `clip()` returns the target clip as soon as a fade starts.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nThe `sha256` and animation list in `defineModelAssets` are copied from the docs recipe, and I didn't recompute the hash from the file in `public/assets`. If the hash is checked and doesn't match, the model will fail to draw.",
